2026-09-23: ublk worker verdict integrity, not a kernel stall repair.

RED: 99 selected Python tests, nine failing assertions, no import/syntax errors.
The standalone shell reduction has parent exit 0 even after a worker's [FAIL]
or fatal helper exit. Fault injection into the unchanged upstream script then
confirms the same behavior with three concurrent workers: three failed device
additions, or three failed removals, followed by stress_04 : [PASS], exit 0.
The actual upstream _check_add_dev, run_io_and_kill_daemon and _show_result
functions run; only device setup/I/O helpers are stubbed. No kernel is exercised
by this injection. Its clean control has no inner failures.

GREEN: match summaries to the actual ublk script's test ID; preserve FAIL/SKIP
records and recognized fatal helper diagnostics. A successful outer wrapper
requires a complete matching summary. Expected block I/O errors are not verdicts.
Multi-phase success records remain legal. Preserve the outer TAP result and
denominator; inner failures instead prevent aggregate all-tests acceptance.
This does not prove every silent worker exited zero: it closes the reproduced
lost-diagnostic paths, not all possible upstream shell-runner defects.

99 selected tests PASS; full K1 tests 238 PASS; ladder tests 240 PASS.
Ruff/diff/status-render checks PASS. gate-changed 52282f0 correctly selects no
Rust crates; it is not recorded as a Rust workspace/clippy run.
122 retained raw ublk flights reparse as 107 PASS, 6 SKIP, 3 TIMEOUT, 6 FAIL.
The six recognized inner failures belong to already-failing generic_01/02;
no historical outcome or receipt is rewritten.

Two fresh serial diagnostic flights reuse the matched existing runtime disks
via QEMU snapshot=on. The original stress_04 workload and 45-second test limit
are unchanged. The retained diagnostic init requests SysRq blocked-task stacks
after the program; both programs exit 0, no blocked tasks are printed, and both
guests power off (reference 3.465313 s; subject 4.656888 s boot uptime).
These are additional PASS observations, NOT an explanation/fix of the old stall.
K04 remains OPEN. No Image, module, original test, or full receipt is replaced.

